🧩 Step 4: Why OSPF Gets Stuck (Real Troubleshooting 🔥)

Now we move to real-world problem solving (this is what companies test)

🧠 Situation

Two routers are connected, but:

👉 They are not reaching FULL state

🖼️ Visual Idea
5
🚨 Common Problems (Very Important)
1️⃣ Hello Timer Mismatch
One router sends Hello every 10 sec
Other expects 5 sec

👉 Result: ❌ No neighbor

2️⃣ Area Mismatch
Router 1 → Area 0
Router 2 → Area 1

👉 ❌ They will NOT connect

3️⃣ Authentication Mismatch
One router has password
Other doesn’t

👉 ❌ Connection fails

4️⃣ MTU Mismatch (VERY IMPORTANT 🔥)

👉 Routers get stuck in:

EXSTART / EXCHANGE state

Why?
Packet size mismatch
5️⃣ Network Type Mismatch
One uses broadcast
Other uses point-to-point

👉 If OSPF fails, check:
H A A M N
H → Hello timer
A → Area
A → Authentication
M → MTU
N → Network type

